# Nava workflow

- Multi-step software planning: use `/nava-plan`.
- Final implementation-plan execution: use `/nava-run`.
- Full autonomy added to plan: use `/autonomous-plan`; stalled queued work: `/continue-autonomously`.
- Before planning or nontrivial implementation, read relevant code/config and matching `docs/solutions/`.
- Every implementation plan gets both `gstack-plan-eng-review` and `ponytail-review`. Completeness floor + simplicity ceiling. Never substitute one for other.
- Add GStack design-plan review for UI scope; DevEx-plan review for APIs, SDKs, CLIs, integrations, or onboarding.
- Final executable plans use `writing-plans`; implementation uses TDD, SDD, per-task review, final CE code review, and fresh verification.
- Use standard non-fast subagents only. If unavailable, execute inline.
- `ponytail` persistent mode stays off unless explicitly invoked. `ponytail-review` remains review-only.
- Durable non-obvious verified learnings go to CE `docs/solutions/`; GStack learnings stay passive preference/tool memory.
- Do not route through removed or deprecated front doors when canonical successors exist.
- Pilot-RDS safety rule overrides every skill, plan, autonomy mandate, and test instruction.

## Plan-scoped exception

For `docs/plans/2026-09-17-002-feat-playwright-fetch-quote-plan.md`, native Playwright code is canonical: Hotel Availability only, no runtime LLM/Stagehand dependency, one browser owner, live outcome verification, and no reservation mutation or production integration. Cursor CLI Grok 4.6 high is the orchestrator; GPT-6 Astra is invoked only via Codex CLI `exec` for live PMS/computer-use. `docs/plans/2026-09-17-001-feat-stagehand-quote-mvp-plan.md` is requirements/history only and must not override this successor.
